  "result": "Perfect. I've completed my Season 2 analysis and prepared for Season 3. Here's what I found and changed:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Key Finding:** Season 2's actual peak was in late September (d270-279, avg 2.481 share), not October (d287-305, avg 0.841 share) as my strategy predicted from Season 1 data. I caught the tail on d281 (2.125 share = 93% of my score) but wasted $1,400 testing six weak streaks and locked 9 PTO days to the wrong month.\n\n**Season 3 Changes:**\n1. **Stop calendar betting** \u2014 respond to actual daily data instead of historical templates\n2. **Reserve capital for multiple peaks** \u2014 test early (April-June, $300), commit only to proven signals\n3. **Commit PTO only 1-2 weeks ahead** \u2014 stay flexible, don't lock 14 days early\n4. **Book the first strong signal you see** \u2014 the real peak announces itself with 3+ consecutive positive days, not advance calendar predictability\n\n**Updated strategy.py** with adaptive streak detection that waits for proven signals before committing capital. **Forum post shared** with analysis that September S2 peak exceeded October by 3x, emphasizing the need for responsive data tracking over planning assumptions.\n\nTarget: 4.0+ fish for Season 3 (competitive top-10), vs. 2.29 in Season 2.",
